{"label":"convex","explanation":"Write P(x)=4x(x²−1/16)(x²−1/4)(x²−9/16)(x²−1). Then f=log(1+P²)+2x² is smooth throughout [-1,1], and f''=4+2(1−P²)(P')²/(1+P²)²+2PP''/(1+P²). We establish |P|<1 and PP''>−2, which imply f''>4−4/(1+P²)≥0.

First, P=(16T₉+24T₇+9T₅−16T₃−33T₁)/1024, where Tₙ are Chebyshev polynomials. Thus |P|≤49/512<1/10 on [-1,1]. For the second bound, set t=x² and B(t)=36864t³−40320t²+10920t−615, so P''=xB(t)/128. On [0,3/4], B has Bernstein coefficients (−615,2115,−2715,447), giving |B|≤2715, |P''|<19, and hence |PP''|<1.9.

For t∈[3/4,1], B's three roots βⱼ lie in (0,3/4), as its signs alternate at 0,1/4,1/2,3/4. Put u=1−t and r=(1,15/16,3/4,7/16,1−β₁,1−β₂,1−β₃). Factoring gives −PP''=K u∏ⱼ(1−u/rⱼ), where K=2157435/32768<66 and S=Σⱼ1/rⱼ=199/35+40872/6849>23/2. All factors are nonnegative, so AM–GM gives −PP''≤K u(1−Su/7)⁷≤(K/S)(7/8)⁸<(132/23)(7/8)⁸<2. Therefore f''>0 throughout the supplied interval: f is strictly convex and not concave."}

